{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/513909-creating-a-monster","id":513909,"title":"Creating a monster","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-14T00:09:58-07:00","id":513909,"title":"Creating a monster","content":"I'm planning a Cheiron Group hunter, one who has the Cortical Adaptation, and a whole raft of slasher merits. <br /> <br /> I want to play him as someone who knows he is a monster, who does what hedies not for him self, but for the sake of society. He's sold his soul to Cheiron Group, essentially. Or at least that's how he sees it. <br /> <br /> Each. 'upgrade ' is another slice of soul gone, and each monster killed (however gruesomely) is a piece redeemed. <br /> <br /> To make this work I need to make him a combat monster. <br /> <br /> Myproblem is that as I was trying to stat up the character, it seemed like a lot of effort for little return.<br /> <br /> My build relied on boosting wits, and sacrificing dex. Then buying a dot in Status(Cheiron Group) and spending three dots in Cortical Adaptation, and burning another one of Atavism (making my dexterity sacrifice worthwhile) . That's 5 of my merit dots gone, and four of them having been spent not getting a direct bonus to combat. I wanted to put dots in Weaponry Monomaniac (2) and Frenzied Assault (1-2) but I'm short.<br /> <br /> On top of this, my Slasher merits would only work when I activated them with willpower. If I (ever) get to 5 dots in Frenzied assault, I'm spending another willpower point to use it once.<br /> <br /> I have ~25 xp to work with, and I'm it off ideas on how to make him as fearsome combat-wise as he will be roleplay-wise. <br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:27:51-07:00","id":528615,"title":"","content":"No one has any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T02:19:28-07:00","id":528666,"title":"","content":"It's dodging the question a bit but you could play him as he becomes a monster, getting weaponry monomaniac and frenzied assault later. It'd give you some contrast at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:12:50-07:00","id":528724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-